<title>MONACO: TENNIS-LEADING ATP PRIZE-MONEY WINNERS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-LEADING ATP PRIZE-MONEY WINNERS.</headline>
<dateline>MONACO 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading prize-money winners issued</p>
<p>by the ATP Tour on Monday:</p>
<p> 1. Pete Sampras (U.S.)		  $3,702,919</p>
<p> 2. Thomas Muster (Austria)	     2,875,496</p>
<p> 3. Yevgeny Kafelnikov (Russia)	 2,682,115</p>
<p> 4. Boris Becker (Germany)		2,438,007</p>
<p> 5. Goran Ivanisevic (Croatia)	  2,195,485</p>
<p> 6. Michael Chang (U.S.)		  2,015,699</p>
<p> 7. Thomas Enqvist (Sweden)	     1,668,547</p>
<p> 8. Andre Agassi (U.S.)		   1,529,928</p>
<p> 9. Richard Krajicek (Netherlands)    1,511,761</p>
<p> 10. Todd Woodbridge (Australia)	1,080,633</p>
<p> 11. Mark Woodforde (Australia)	 1,069,527</p>
<p> 12. Paul Haarhuis (Netherlands)	  964,086</p>
<p> 13. Wayne Ferreira (South Africa)	961,020</p>
<p> 14. Marc Rosset (Switzerland)	    903,439</p>
<p> 15. Todd Martin (U.S.)		     868,636</p>
<p> 16. Jakob Hlasek (Switzerland)	   838,383</p>
<p> 17. Marcelo Rios (Chile)		   825,678</p>
<p> 18. Jim Courier (U.S.)		     815,852</p>
<p> 19. Alberto Costa (Spain)		  801,771</p>
<p> 20. Jan Siemerink (Netherlands)	  753,881</p>
